{"strongs": "H6305", "word": "פְּדָיָהוּ", "translit": "pe.da.yah", "root": "פדיהו", "morph": "N:N-M-P", "pos": "proper name, masculine", "gloss": "hath ransomed", "definition": "פְּדָיָהוּ , פְּדָיָה proper name, masculine ( ׳ י hath ransomed ; in late Assyrian Padâma, Hilpr Univ. Pa, Exp. ix. 27, 68 ); — פְּדָיָה : 1. father-in-law of Josiah 2Kgs 23:36 , but ᵐ5 Εδειλ ( ᵐ5 L Ιερεμιας , from v 2Kgs 23:31 ). 2. father of Zerubbabel 1Chr 3:18 ; 1Chr 3:19 . 3. a. Neh 3:25 . \\ \\ b. Neh 8:4 . 4. Benjamite Neh 11:7 . 5. Levite Neh 13:13 . 6. פְּדָיָהוּ , Manassite 1Chr 27:20 — ᵐ5 (except 1 ) Φα ( λ ) δαιας , etc.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6532')\">BDB6532</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H6305')\">H6305</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6531')\">BDB6531</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB6533')\">BDB6533</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>פְּדָיָהוּ</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>פְּדָיָה</bdbheb> <b>proper name, masculine</b> (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <highlight>hath ransomed</highlight>; in late Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>Padâma,</highlight></transliteration> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hilpr')\">Hilpr<sup>Univ. Pa, Exp. ix. 27, 68</sup></lookup>); — <bdbheb>פְּדָיָה</bdbheb>: <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> father-in-law of Josiah <ref ref=\"2Kgs 23:36\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"36\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"36\" onclick=\"bcv(12,23,36)\">2Kgs 23:36</ref>, but <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Εδειλ</grk> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb><reflink><sup>L</sup></reflink></lookup> <grk>Ιερεμιας</grk>, from v<ref ref=\"2Kgs 23:31\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(12,23,31)\">2Kgs 23:31</ref>). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> father of Zerubbabel <ref ref=\"1Chr 3:18\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(13,3,18)\">1Chr 3:1